        "sourceId": "st_john-estate-beverhoutberg-estate",
        "label": "Beverhoutberg; Estate about 1/4 mile southwest of Adrian, St. John; taking its name from 545-foot hill, so named for John (von) Beverhout, a n early planter of distinction, who, as Militia-Captain, defended Peter Duurloo's plantation in the slave revolt of 1733, and founded a n influentinl family. The name is derived from the Dutch words, \"Bever\" (benver), and \" Hout \" (wood). It has been variously corrupted; as, Beverhoudt, lieverhoud, Bevenhoul, Beverhoubt, etc. The estate is shown by Oxholm, Dewitz, Zabriskie, B. A. 2452, etc. , but not on T. 3772. -Knox. , p. 72 f; Westergaard, pp. 38, 169, 173. Scorpion survey shows buildings of \" Beverhoudtberg \" on stream, southeast of 5454%. hill mentioned.",
