        "source": "geographicIndex",
        "sourceId": "st_john-bay-calvary-bay",
        "label": "Calvary Bay; 370 yards wide, 820 yards long, sheltered, in southwest part of St. John I s l a n d. 4. B. Long known by the hybrid English-Spanish name, \"Great Cruz Bay. \" St. John having been settled by the Dutch, the original name doubtless was \" Groot-Kruis Bay \"; or Danish, '' StoreKrys '' or \" Store-Kors \" Bay. Oldendorp and Dewitz give it as '' Gross-Cruxbay '' (Ger. ); Oxholm, as \" StoreCruytz, \" and the Derrotero, 'I Bahia Grande de la Cruz. \" Since Crue Bay has come to refer to the post omce on Little Crue Bay, Q. v. , to avoid confusion, the name of the bay has been conformed to that of the post oflice, dropping altogether the name \"Great Cruz. \" Since this last refers to the \" Great Cross of Calvary, \" the name I' Calvary Bay \" was favored by several well-informed authorities and indorsed by the late President Harding, in compliment to Calvary Baptist Church, of Washington, D. C. , of which he was an honored attendant.",
        "confidence": 0.8
      }
    ],
    "searchText": "st john bay calvary bay calvary bay bay st john calvary bay 370 yards wide 820 yards long sheltered in southwest part of st john i s l a n d 4 b long known by the hybrid english spanish name great cruz bay st john having been settled by the dutch the original name doubtless was groot kruis bay or danish storekrys or store kors bay oldendorp and dewitz give it as gross cruxbay ger oxholm as storecruytz and the derrotero i bahia grande de la cruz since crue bay has come to refer to the post omce on little crue bay q v to avoid confusion the name of the bay has been conformed to that of the post oflice dropping altogether the name great cruz since this last refers to the great cross of calvary the name i calvary bay was favored by several well informed authorities and indorsed by the late president harding in compliment to calvary baptist church of washington d c of which he was an honored attendant"
  },
