re white, 14, 254 (96. 5 per cent) colored; dehsity, about 208 to the square mile. English is the prevailing language, although there is considerable use of Danish, Spanish, French, and the Creole patois. The name bestowed by Columbus, in its Spunish form \"Santa Cruz, \" Latin, \"Sancta Crux, \" was transmuted during the French oacupution (1651-1733) into 'I Sainte Croix. \" VarioUB hybrid forms occur, as, '' St. Crux, \" \" Sanct Croix, \" etc. , but \" Saint Croix '' gained vogue with the Dan& and Americana, and is now official.",
